csv:     section3-gamma-vs-composition.csv
source:  ../source.pdf p.9 (journal page 308), the unnumbered table in sect. 3
anchor:  Some values of
anchor:  reduction
anchor:  deduced below from curves given by

# THIS TABLE FEEDS SHIPPED CODE. src/arty/fragmentation.py carries gamma = 47
# for WDSS-1 (interpolated inside the 0.1 C -> 0.25 C segment) and gamma = 65
# for the legacy grade (anchored just under the 0.45 C row's 67). Both read the
# gamma column below, and nothing else in this table.
#
# TRANSCRIPTION IS VERIFIED. Every cell was read off source.pdf page 9 at
# 420 dpi during the Phase-2.5 admissibility gate (ledger sect. 17). This
# supersedes the pre-2026-07-25 OCR, which had gamma(0.1 C) = 32 and labelled
# the third row 0.2 C; both are wrong and both reached derivation.md before
# being corrected.
#
# carbon_pct IS DERIVED, NOT TRANSCRIBED. The page labels the rows "iron",
# "steel 0.1 C", "0.25 C", "0.45 C". The 0.0 on the iron row is this repo's
# reading of "iron" as nominally carbon-free; the page states no number.

# --- what holds -------------------------------------------------------------
# Three of the five columns are ordered, which is what catches a row swap or an
# off-by-one read of the interleaved rows.
monotonic: carbon_pct increasing
monotonic: reduction_in_area decreasing
monotonic: P_F_kg_per_mm2 increasing
monotonic: gamma increasing

# P_2 is NOT monotonic (34, 42, 45, 38) -- the 0.45 C row turns it over. That is
# on the page; do not "fix" it.
total: P_2_kg_per_mm2 == 159 within 0.5

# --- what does NOT hold, and it is the point of this file --------------------
# The page states its own closure two lines above the table:
#
#     gamma ~ 160 P_2 / P_F (1 + s_F)
#
# with P_F "the true stress and s_F the plastic strain at fracture" (p. 307,
# anchor "where P_F is the true stress"). The table tabulates P_2, P_F and a
# "reduction in area" column, and the sentence introducing it says values "of
# P_2, P_F, s_F have been deduced below" -- so reduction in area is the
# tabulated stand-in for s_F.
#
# THE COLUMN DOES NOT REPRODUCE. Taking s_F as the reduction in area directly
# gives 55.0 / 56.5 / 55.2 / 47.2; taking s_F = ln(1/(1-RA)), the true plastic
# strain, gives 36.3 / 43.6 / 45.1 / 40.2. Both are nearly FLAT, while the
# printed gamma column rises 20 -> 42 -> 53 -> 67, a factor of 3.35. The
# implied proportionality constant would have to run 58 -> 227.
#
# The rising trend is precisely what this repo consumes -- gamma = 47 is an
# interpolation ALONG that trend. So the failure is not cosmetic.
#
# This is not expressible as a passing check, and it is not a transcription
# defect: the digits are confirmed against the page. It is either a fuller
# derivation Mott did not print (he writes "~", and says N "can only be
# guessed"), or an inconsistency in the 1947 paper. Deciding which is a
# modelling question, not a librarian one -- registered as a blocking finding
# against src/arty/fragmentation.py. Residuals are pinned, so that a future
# re-extraction that moves a digit moves them too, in:
#   experiment/fragmentation-field/challenges/source-data-audit/checks/
#     mott-1947-gamma-and-length-closure.py
